course: dictionary
lesson: 5387
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Knot is a word with more than one meaning, so the sentence around it is your best clue. As a noun, a knot is a place where string, rope or ribbon is tied around itself or another piece. As a verb, to knot means to tie a knot or to get tangled.
explain: «Male weaver birds weave hanging nests from grass strips, tying knots with beak and feet.» The word tying tells you that a knot is a tie made in grass. Swap in your meaning: "tying a tie with beak and feet" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Knot can also mean a tight, uncomfortable feeling. In «a knot in my stomach», the feeling is not a real rope. Nerves make you feel tight and tangled inside, so the sentence tells you that knot means worry here.
fact: A knot is a place where string, rope or ribbon is tied around itself or around another piece.
fact: «Knotted strings called quipu» were used to keep records, so people once kept information by tying knots.
fact: Ships, boats, planes and wind are measured in knots: one knot is one nautical mile per hour.
fact: A knot can also be a hard, dark round spot in wood, where a branch once grew.
fact: «Tie the knot» means to get married, and «a knot in my stomach» means a tight, worried feeling.
exercise: «She tied a tight knot in the ribbon.» What does knot mean here? | A worried feeling | A unit of speed for boats | A hard, dark spot in wood | *A place where the ribbon is tied around itself
exercise: «The yacht sailed at ten knots.» What are knots measuring here? | *Speed | The length of the rope | Weight | The colour of the sail
exercise: «I had a knot in my stomach before the test.» What does the knot show? | Hunger | A tied rope | *Worry or nerves | Tiredness after a long walk
test: «They had no writing as we know it, but kept records with knotted strings called quipu.» What were the quipu used for? | Making soup | *Keeping records | Catching fish | Climbing mountains
test: «The fishing line got knotted round the rock.» What does knotted mean here? | Hard and dark | Pulled very quickly | Hung up to dry | *Tangled
exam: «The carpenter sanded the plank and found a dark knot where a branch had grown.» What is the knot? | *A hard, dark round spot in wood | A tangled lump of thread | A way to tie a boat to the dock | A unit of speed for ships
